DIAG: ath12k: print the memory chunks handed to the firmware

Temporary, not for upstream.

The Q6's own crash record says it took a NULL dereference:

  :Excep :0 Exception detected  PName:wlan0  TName:WLAN BE
  SP : 0x4ca52a00  FP : 0x4ca52a28  PC : 0xb01c2a48
  SSR : 0x01970170  BADVA : 0x00000000  LR : 0xb01c2a10

BADVA 0 means it dereferenced a pointer that was zero, and the pointers
the host supplies are the memory chunks negotiated over QMI. The loop
that sends them already logs each one, but at ATH12K_DBG_QMI, which is
off. Raise it so the addresses are visible.

Signed-off-by: Hideo Sumi <hideo.sumi@mugops.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -2396,11 +2396,11 @@
 			req->mem_seg[i].addr = ab->qmi.target_mem[i].paddr;
 			req->mem_seg[i].size = ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size;
 			req->mem_seg[i].type = ab->qmi.target_mem[i].type;
-			ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_QMI,
-				   "qmi req mem_seg[%d] %pad %u %u\n", i,
-				   &ab->qmi.target_mem[i].paddr,
-				   ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size,
-				   ab->qmi.target_mem[i].type);
+			ath12k_warn(ab,
+				    "DBG: mem_seg[%d] paddr=%pad size=%u type=%u\n", i,
+				    &ab->qmi.target_mem[i].paddr,
+				    ab->qmi.target_mem[i].size,
+				    ab->qmi.target_mem[i].type);
 		}
 	}
 
